The previous design looks too AI-generated and too much like a generic futuristic AI SaaS landing page.

Redesign it to remove the "AI-generated website" aesthetic.

Keep the core concept of a cinematic 3D scrolling experience, but make the design feel like it was art-directed by a human creative director and built for a serious scientific computing research platform.

DO NOT simply make it more futuristic.

Make it more restrained, unusual, editorial and technically believable.

REMOVE:

- giant gradient headlines
- excessive purple/blue neon
- excessive glowing cards
- glassmorphism
- floating holographic panels
- generic AI interface elements
- excessive rounded cards
- excessive badges
- fake-looking technical statistics
- robot/AI imagery
- generic "future of AI" language
- unnecessary icons
- decorative circuit-board patterns
- excessive borders
- excessive shadows
- symmetrical card grids
- stock-looking illustrations

VISUAL DIRECTION:

Think:

experimental scientific visualization
+
high-end editorial website
+
research laboratory interface
+
cinematic 3D installation

NOT:

AI startup landing page
NOT:
cyberpunk dashboard
NOT:
crypto website
NOT:
medical SaaS template

LAYOUT:

Use asymmetry.

Do not center every section.

Allow large areas of empty space.

Use unusual compositions where appropriate:
- text positioned at edges
- large 3D scene occupying most of the viewport
- small technical annotations
- oversized but restrained typography
- sections that overlap slightly
- visual elements entering from outside the viewport

The page should feel composed rather than generated from a UI component library.

TYPOGRAPHY:

Use typography as an editorial design element.

Prefer:
- strong grotesk / modern sans-serif
- restrained font weights
- small uppercase technical labels
- large text only when necessary

Avoid:
- gradient text
- glowing text
- excessive bold typography

COLOR:

Use an almost black / graphite foundation.

Primary text:
off-white rather than pure white.

Accent:
muted mint.

Secondary accent:
very restrained violet.

The accents should appear primarily inside the scientific visualization.

The UI itself should mostly remain neutral.

3D:

The 3D scene is the star.

Create an abstract field of particles that behaves like a physical computational system.

It should NOT look like:
- an AI brain
- an atom
- a galaxy
- DNA
- a hologram
- a neural network illustration

Instead, create something that looks like:

a mathematical field becoming organized.

The particles should transition between states as the user scrolls.

STATE 01:
disordered particles

STATE 02:
particles flowing into streams

STATE 03:
streams forming an abstract topology

STATE 04:
topology splitting into computational pathways

STATE 05:
pathways interacting

STATE 06:
structure collapsing into interpretable signals

The transitions should feel physically continuous.

IMPORTANT:

Do not put a giant glass card behind the 3D visualization.

Let the 3D scene occupy the environment itself.

SCROLL EXPERIENCE:

Make scrolling feel like controlling a scientific simulation.

The camera should move through the environment.

The user should not feel like they are scrolling through 10 marketing sections.

Instead:

SCROLL
→ simulation state changes
→ camera moves
→ data reorganizes
→ information is revealed

CONTENT STYLE:

Replace marketing language with precise language.

Instead of:

"Unlock the power of AI"

Use:

"Biomedical data is rarely simple."

Instead of:

"Next-generation intelligence"

Use:

"Different models expose different structures in the data."

Instead of:

"AI-powered insights"

Use:

"Prediction, consensus and model sensitivity."

Instead of:

"Revolutionary quantum AI"

Use:

"Quantum models evaluated alongside established classical baselines."

The writing should sound like a research platform.

SECTION DESIGN:

HERO:

Almost empty.

VITALIS
small technical identifier

Then:

HYBRID INTELLIGENCE
FOR EARLY DISEASE SCREENING

Minimal supporting text.

Let the 3D scene dominate.

DATA SECTION:

Do not create a conventional card.

Use the particle field itself to communicate complexity.

Small annotations appear around the visualization.

PATTERN SECTION:

The particle system becomes organized.

Use one short statement:

"Structure emerges from complexity."

COMPUTATION:

Instead of two large cards saying CLASSICAL and QUANTUM, integrate the labels into the 3D computational environment.

Small labels identify pathways.

CLASSICAL
LR · RF · RBF SVM

QUANTUM
QSVM · VQC

CONVERGENCE:

Let both pathways visually meet.

Use minimal text.

"One dataset.
Multiple computational perspectives."

BENCHMARK:

Make this look like a research figure rather than a marketing chart.

Use thin lines, precise axes, restrained typography and actual-looking scientific visualization.

EXPLAINABILITY:

Avoid generic AI explanation cards.

Show feature signals appearing and disappearing from the computational field.

Use small technical labels.

RESEARCH:

Make this feel almost like an interactive research paper.

Include:

RESEARCH QUESTION

METHOD

DATA

MODELS

EVALUATION

LIMITATIONS

REPRODUCIBILITY

FINAL:

Very minimal.

VITALIS

"Explore the intelligence behind the prediction."

Do not add unnecessary visual effects.

OVERALL PRINCIPLE:

The design should look LESS like:

"AI generated a futuristic website"

and MORE like:

"A highly skilled creative technologist designed an experimental scientific computing interface."

The result should be sophisticated enough that the visual design itself does not immediately reveal that an AI website builder created it.